---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Search 3,000 documents" hint="A small search engine over 3,000 generated documents, with a real inverted index, split over shards. Change how the query is analysed, intersected and ranked, and watch the postings it has to read.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with <b>the bloom filter</b>, an AND query on 8 shards, with stop words kept: the word <b>the</b> has a posting list of about 2,600 documents, so the query reads about <b>3,000 postings</b> to find <b>23</b> documents. Tick <b>Intersect shortest list first</b> and <b>Skip pointers</b>: it reads only about <b>600</b>, because the 40 documents with <b>bloom</b> are checked in the long lists by jumping, not by reading.</li>
    <li>Tick <b>Remove stop words</b> instead: the list for <b>the</b> is gone, so the same query reads about <b>300</b> postings, and the engine now matches 30 documents. Then change <b>Query type</b> to <b>exact phrase</b>: the engine has to check the word <b>positions</b> as well, and only documents with the words side by side remain.</li>
    <li>Raise <b>Shards</b> from 1 to 16. Each shard has less to read, so the time falls from <b>5.1 ms</b> to <b>1.6 ms</b> at 8 shards, but at 16 it is slightly worse again, because the answer waits for the <b>slowest</b> shard and a few shards are always slow. Choose <b>answer without the slow shards</b> at 8 shards: it takes <b>1.4 ms</b>, but only <b>8 of the real top 10</b> come back.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg sxb" data-sxb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Query <select class="pg-in" data-q></select></label>
      <label>Query type <select class="pg-in" data-type>
        <option value="term">single term (the last word)</option>
        <option value="and" selected>AND of all the words</option>
        <option value="phrase">exact phrase</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Ranking <select class="pg-in" data-rank>
        <option value="none">none (first 10 by document id)</option>
        <option value="tfidf">TF-IDF</option>
        <option value="bm25" selected>BM25</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Shards <select class="pg-in" data-s>
        <option value="1">1</option><option value="2">2</option><option value="4">4</option><option value="8" selected>8</option><option value="16">16</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>When a shard is slow <select class="pg-in" data-drop>
        <option value="wait" selected>wait for every shard</option>
        <option value="drop">answer without the slow shards</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label class="sx-check"><input type="checkbox" data-stop /> Remove stop words</label>
      <label class="sx-check"><input type="checkbox" data-stem checked /> Stem words</label>
      <label class="sx-check"><input type="checkbox" data-short /> Intersect shortest list first</label>
      <label class="sx-check"><input type="checkbox" data-skip /> Skip pointers</label>
      <label class="sx-check"><input type="checkbox" data-early /> Early termination (block maximums)</label>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-note" data-terms aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Postings read</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Documents scored</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Latency</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Top 10 complete</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="sx-cols">
      <div>
        <h4 class="sx-h">Time on each shard</h4>
        <div class="sx-bars" data-bars role="list" aria-label="Time spent by each shard"></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4 class="sx-h">Top 10 results</h4>
        <ol class="sx-res" data-res aria-label="Top results"></ol>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: documents go to a shard by a hash of the id, and each shard has its own inverted index with word positions. A shard returns its best 10 and the coordinator merges them. Scores use global document counts, as if a first round collected them. Skip pointers sit every 8 postings, a small scale for a small corpus. Latency is 0.15 ms plus 0.0015 ms per posting, 0.0004 ms per position and 0.01 ms per scored document, times a fixed speed factor per shard (1 to 3.2, from garbage collection and merges), plus a small merge cost. The slow-shard option drops shards that take more than 1.5 times the median. Block maximums are exact: they skip only documents that could not enter the top 10.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .sx-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .sx-cols { display: grid; gap: 16px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(260px, 100%), 1fr)); margin-top: 12px; }
  .sx-h { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  .sx-bars { display: grid; gap: 3px; }
  .sx-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4.2rem 1fr 4rem; gap: 6px; align-items: center; font: .78rem ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .sx-bar[hidden] { display: none; }
  .sx-track { height: 9px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--surface-2, var(--accent-soft)); overflow: hidden; }
  .sx-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; transition: width .25s; }
  .sx-bar.slow .sx-fill { background: var(--role-4, var(--accent)); }
  .sx-bar.cut .sx-fill { background: var(--bad); }
  .sx-bar.cut { color: var(--bad-text, var(--bad)); }
  .sx-res { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.6rem; display: grid; gap: 3px; font-size: .84rem; min-height: 12em; }
  .sx-res li[hidden] { display: none; }
  .sx-res .sc { font: .78rem ui-monospace, monospace; color: var(--muted); margin-right: 6px; }
  .sx-res b { color: var(--text); background: var(--accent-soft); border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 2px; }
  .sx-res .tx { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sxb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // ---- core: corpus, inverted index, search ----
    const DOCS = 3000; const K = 10; const BLOCK = 8;
    const SYNTH = { count: 250, mul: 7, add: 3, endings: ['m', 'n', 'r', 'l', 'k'] }; // made-up rare words built from syllables
    const BLOOM_RANK = 230; // frequency rank where the rare word "bloom" is inserted
    const FW_NOUN = [0.7, 0.3]; // singular / plural share
    const ZIPF = { offset: 3, exp: 1.6 }; // word frequency ~ 1 / (rank + 3)^1.6
    const DOC_LEN = { min: 15, maxExtra: 120, mean: 28 }; // tokens: 15 plus an exponential tail with mean 28, capped at 120
    const STOP_SHARE = 0.3; const STOP_SKEW = 1.6; // share of tokens that are stop words, and how strongly the first ones dominate
    const STEM_MIN = { ing: 5, ed: 4, s: 3 }; // shortest word each suffix rule applies to (exclusive)
    const BM25 = { k1: 1.2, b: 0.75 };
    const BM_BLOCK = 8; // postings per block-maximum entry
    const EPS = 1e-9; // float tolerance when comparing scores
    const COST_MS = { base: 0.15, posting: 0.0015, position: 0.0004, score: 0.01 }; // simulated shard time per unit of work
    const COORD_MS = { base: 0.2, perShard: 0.004 }; // coordinator merge time
    const DEADLINE_X_MEDIAN = 1.5; // drop shards slower than 1.5x the median
    const WASTE_X = 1.8; // postings read beyond this multiple of the best plan count as wasteful
    const BAR_MIN_MS = 0.01; // floor for the bar chart scale
    const SNIPPET = { before: 4, len: 12 }; // tokens shown around the first hit
    // Numerical Recipes LCG
    let seed = 7; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const STOP = ['the', 'of', 'and', 'to', 'a', 'in', 'is', 'for', 'on', 'with'];
    const STOPSET = new Set(STOP);
    const forms = (b: string) => { const es = /(x|ch|sh)$/.test(b) ? 'es' : 's'; return [b, b + es, b + 'ed', b + 'ing']; };
    const ORDER = 'list test work link point open read log map send host post pack pull push watch mark lock limit print need search crawl index load track sort build match fetch stream record filter token cluster segment document term field engine shard rank inverted replica'.split(' ');
    const NOUNS: Record<string, string[]> = { engine: ['engine', 'engines'], replica: ['replica', 'replicas'], inverted: ['inverted'] };
    const UNITS: string[][] = ORDER.map((w) => NOUNS[w] || forms(w));
    const SYL = ['ka', 'vo', 'ri', 'tem', 'lu', 'nor', 'pi', 'zan', 'del', 'mu', 'qua', 'fen'];
    for (let i = 0; i < SYNTH.count; i++) UNITS.push([SYL[i % SYL.length] + SYL[Math.floor(i / SYL.length) % SYL.length] + SYL[(i * SYNTH.mul + SYNTH.add) % SYL.length] + SYNTH.endings[i % SYNTH.endings.length]]);
    UNITS.splice(BLOOM_RANK, 0, ['bloom', 'blooms']);
    const FW = [0.4, 0.25, 0.15, 0.2];
    const cum: number[] = []; { let s = 0; UNITS.forEach((_, i) => { s += 1 / Math.pow(i + ZIPF.offset, ZIPF.exp); cum.push(s); }); }
    const pickUnit = (u: number) => { const t = u * cum[cum.length - 1]; let lo = 0, hi = cum.length - 1; while (lo < hi) { const m = (lo + hi) >> 1; if (cum[m] < t) lo = m + 1; else hi = m; } return lo; };
    const pickForm = (f: string[], u: number) => { const n = f.length; if (n === 1) return f[0]; const w = n === FW.length ? FW : FW_NOUN; let a = 0; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { a += w[i]; if (u < a) return f[i]; } return f[n - 1]; };
    const PHR: [string, string, number][] = [['bloom', 'filter', 0.008], ['inverted', 'index', 0.04], ['search', 'engine', 0.04], ['shard', 'replica', 0.03]];
    const corpus: string[][] = Array.from({ length: DOCS }, () => {
      const len = DOC_LEN.min + Math.min(DOC_LEN.maxExtra, Math.floor(-Math.log(1 - rnd()) * DOC_LEN.mean)); const t: string[] = [];
      for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) t.push(rnd() < STOP_SHARE ? STOP[Math.floor(Math.pow(rnd(), STOP_SKEW) * STOP.length)] : pickForm(UNITS[pickUnit(rnd())], rnd()));
      for (const [a, b, p] of PHR) if (rnd() < p) { const at = Math.floor(rnd() * (len - 1)); t[at] = a; t[at + 1] = b; }
      return t;
    });
    const stem = (w: string) => { if (w.length > STEM_MIN.ing && w.endsWith('ing')) return w.slice(0, -3); if (w.length > STEM_MIN.ed && w.endsWith('ed')) return w.slice(0, -2); if (/(x|ch|sh)es$/.test(w)) return w.slice(0, -2); if (w.length > STEM_MIN.s && w.endsWith('s') && !w.endsWith('ss')) return w.slice(0, -1); return w; };
    // integer hash (murmur3-style finalizer) to spread documents over shards
    const mix = (id: number) => { let h = Math.imul(id + 1, 2654435761) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 15; h = Math.imul(h, 2246822519) >>> 0; h ^= h >>> 13; return h >>> 0; };
    const cache = new Map<string, any[]>();
    function build(S: number, doStem: boolean, doStop: boolean) {
      const key = `${S}|${doStem}|${doStop}`; const hit = cache.get(key); if (hit) return hit;
      const shards: any[] = Array.from({ length: S }, () => ({ terms: new Map(), len: new Map(), n: 0, total: 0, bm: new Map() }));
      corpus.forEach((toks, id) => {
        const sh = shards[mix(id) % S]; sh.n++; sh.total += toks.length; sh.len.set(id, toks.length);
        toks.forEach((w, pos) => {
          if (doStop && STOPSET.has(w)) return; const t = doStem ? stem(w) : w; // positions keep their gaps where a stop word was removed
          let e = sh.terms.get(t); if (!e) { e = { d: [], p: [] }; sh.terms.set(t, e); }
          if (e.d[e.d.length - 1] !== id) { e.d.push(id); e.p.push([]); } e.p[e.p.length - 1].push(pos);
        });
      });
      cache.set(key, shards); return shards;
    }
    const PRESETS = ['the bloom filter', 'the search index', 'searching indexed shards', 'inverted index', 'the shard replica', 'search engine'];
    function analyse(text: string, doStem: boolean, doStop: boolean) {
      const out: { term: string; off: number }[] = []; text.split(' ').forEach((w, off) => { if (doStop && STOPSET.has(w)) return; out.push({ term: doStem ? stem(w) : w, off }); });
      return out;
    }
    function contrib(rank: string, g: any, df: number, tf: number, dl: number) {
      if (rank === 'tfidf') return (1 + Math.log(tf)) * Math.log(1 + g.n / df); // raw tf keeps growing, and long documents win
      const idf = Math.log(1 + (g.n - df + 0.5) / (df + 0.5)); return (idf * (tf * (BM25.k1 + 1))) / (tf + BM25.k1 * ((1 - BM25.b) + (BM25.b * dl) / g.avg)); // BM25: tf saturates and length is normalised
    }
    function stats(cfg: any) { const one = build(1, cfg.stem, cfg.stop)[0]; return { n: one.n, avg: one.total / one.n, df: (t: string) => (one.terms.get(t) ? one.terms.get(t).d.length : 0) }; }
    const noCost = () => ({ scanned: 0, positions: 0, matched: 0, scored: 0, skipped: 0 });
    function searchShard(sh: any, qterms: any[], o: any, g: any) {
      const cost = noCost();
      let lists: any[] = qterms.map((t) => ({ ...t, e: sh.terms.get(t.term) }));
      if (!lists.length || lists.some((l) => !l.e)) return { hits: [] as any[], cost };
      if (o.shortest) lists.sort((a, b) => a.e.d.length - b.e.d.length);
      const ranked = o.rank !== 'none';
      if (ranked && o.early) lists.forEach((l) => { // the best score in each block of 8 postings, as if stored at index time
        const k = o.rank + l.term; let bm = sh.bm.get(k);
        if (!bm) { bm = []; const df = g.df(l.term); l.e.d.forEach((id: number, i: number) => { const c = contrib(o.rank, g, df, l.e.p[i].length, sh.len.get(id)); const b = Math.floor(i / BM_BLOCK); if (!(bm[b] >= c)) bm[b] = c; }); sh.bm.set(k, bm); }
        l.bm = bm;
      });
      const ptr = lists.map(() => 0); const hits: any[] = []; let thr = -1;
      const inOrder = lists.map((_, i) => i).sort((a, b) => lists[a].off - lists[b].off);
      const advance = (li: number, target: number) => { // first posting >= target in list li, counting every posting touched
        const d = lists[li].e.d; let p = ptr[li];
        if (o.skips) while (p + BLOCK < d.length && d[p + BLOCK] <= target) { p += BLOCK; cost.scanned++; }
        while (p < d.length && d[p] < target) { p++; cost.scanned++; }
        ptr[li] = p; return p < d.length ? d[p] : -1;
      };
      const lead = lists[0].e.d;
      while (ptr[0] < lead.length) {
        if (o.type === 'term' && ranked && o.early && hits.length === K) { // skip a whole block that cannot beat the 10th best
          const b = Math.floor(ptr[0] / BM_BLOCK); if (lists[0].bm[b] < thr - EPS && ptr[0] % BM_BLOCK === 0) { ptr[0] = (b + 1) * BM_BLOCK; cost.scanned++; cost.skipped++; continue; }
        }
        const id = lead[ptr[0]]; cost.scanned++; let ok = true;
        for (let li = 1; li < lists.length; li++) { if (advance(li, id) !== id) { ok = false; break; } }
        ptr[0]++;
        if (!ok) continue;
        if (o.type === 'phrase' && lists.length > 1) { // the positions must line up with the offsets in the query
          const first = lists[0].e.p[ptr[0] - 1]; let found = false;
          for (const p0 of first) { cost.positions++; let all = true; for (let li = 1; li < lists.length; li++) { const need = p0 + (lists[li].off - lists[0].off); cost.positions++; if (!lists[li].e.p[ptr[li]].includes(need)) { all = false; break; } } if (all) { found = true; break; } }
          if (!found) continue;
        }
        cost.matched++;
        if (!ranked) { hits.push({ id, score: 0 }); if (hits.length === K) break; continue; } // no ranking: any 10 matches will do, so stop
        if (o.early && hits.length === K && o.type !== 'term') { let ub = 0; lists.forEach((l, li) => { ub += l.bm[Math.floor((li === 0 ? ptr[0] - 1 : ptr[li]) / BM_BLOCK)]; }); if (ub < thr - EPS) { cost.skipped++; continue; } }
        let s = 0; for (const li of inOrder) { const l = lists[li]; const i = li === 0 ? ptr[0] - 1 : ptr[li]; s += contrib(o.rank, g, g.df(l.term), l.e.p[i].length, sh.len.get(id)); } // always added in query order, so ties are exact
        cost.scored++;
        if (hits.length < K) { hits.push({ id, score: s }); if (hits.length === K) { hits.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score || a.id - b.id); thr = hits[K - 1].score; } }
        else if (s > thr || (s === thr && id < hits[K - 1].id)) { hits[K - 1] = { id, score: s }; hits.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score || a.id - b.id); thr = hits[K - 1].score; }
      }
      if (ranked) hits.sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score || a.id - b.id);
      return { hits, cost };
    }
    const SPEED = [1, 1.1, 1, 1.9, 1.05, 1, 1.15, 1, 3.2, 1.1, 1, 1.2, 1, 1.05, 2.4, 1];
    const msOf = (c: any) => COST_MS.base + COST_MS.posting * c.scanned + COST_MS.position * c.positions + COST_MS.score * c.scored;
    function query(S: number, cfg: any) {
      const shards = build(S, cfg.stem, cfg.stop); const g = stats(cfg); const qt = analyse(cfg.q, cfg.stem, cfg.stop);
      if (cfg.type === 'term') qt.splice(0, qt.length - 1);
      const per = shards.map((sh, i) => { const r = searchShard(sh, qt, cfg, g); return { ...r, ms: msOf(r.cost) * SPEED[i] }; });
      const coord = COORD_MS.base + COORD_MS.perShard * S; const med = per.map((p) => p.ms).sort((a, b) => a - b)[S >> 1];
      const deadline = cfg.drop ? DEADLINE_X_MEDIAN * med : Infinity; const used = per.map((p) => p.ms <= deadline);
      const merged = per.flatMap((p, i) => (used[i] ? p.hits : [])).sort((a, b) => (cfg.rank === 'none' ? a.id - b.id : b.score - a.score || a.id - b.id)).slice(0, K);
      const sum = (f: string) => per.reduce((a, p) => a + (p.cost as any)[f], 0);
      return { per, qt, g, used, merged, deadline, ms: Math.min(Math.max(...per.map((p) => p.ms)), deadline) + coord, scanned: sum('scanned'), positions: sum('positions'), matched: sum('matched'), scored: sum('scored'), skipped: sum('skipped') };
    }
    // ---- end core ----

    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value; const chk = (s: string) => q<HTMLInputElement>(s).checked;
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    PRESETS.forEach((p) => { const o = document.createElement('option'); o.value = p; o.textContent = p; q('[data-q]').append(o); });
    const barsEl = q('[data-bars]');
    const bars = Array.from({ length: SPEED.length }, (_, i) => { // one bar per possible shard
      const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'sx-bar'; row.setAttribute('role', 'listitem');
      const name = document.createElement('span'); name.textContent = `shard ${i + 1}`;
      const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'sx-track'; const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'sx-fill'; track.append(fill);
      const ms = document.createElement('span'); row.append(name, track, ms); barsEl.append(row); return { row, fill, ms };
    });
    const resEl = q('[data-res]');
    const rows = Array.from({ length: K }, () => { const li = document.createElement('li'); const sc = document.createElement('span'); sc.className = 'sc'; const tx = document.createElement('span'); tx.className = 'tx'; li.append(sc, tx); resEl.append(li); return { li, sc, tx }; });

    function draw() {
      const cfg = { q: sel('[data-q]'), type: sel('[data-type]'), rank: sel('[data-rank]'), stem: chk('[data-stem]'), stop: chk('[data-stop]'), shortest: chk('[data-short]'), skips: chk('[data-skip]'), early: chk('[data-early]'), drop: sel('[data-drop]') === 'drop' };
      const S = Number(sel('[data-s]'));
      const r = query(S, cfg);
      const one = query(1, { ...cfg, drop: false });
      const truth = query(1, { ...cfg, drop: false, early: false, shortest: false, skips: false }).merged;
      const best = query(S, { ...cfg, shortest: true, skips: true });
      const have = new Set(r.merged.map((h: any) => h.id)); const complete = truth.filter((h: any) => have.has(h.id)).length;
      const usedN = r.used.filter(Boolean).length;
      q('[data-terms]').textContent = r.qt.length ? 'Terms looked up in the index: ' + r.qt.map((t: any) => `${t.term} (${fmt(r.g.df(t.term))} documents)`).join(', ') + (cfg.type === 'term' ? '. A single-term query uses only the last word.' : '.') : 'Every word of this query is a stop word, so nothing is left to look up.';
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = fmt(r.scanned);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `best possible here: ${fmt(best.scanned)}${r.positions ? ` · ${fmt(r.positions)} positions checked` : ''}`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = cfg.rank === 'none' ? 'none' : fmt(r.scored);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = cfg.rank === 'none' ? `${fmt(r.matched)} matches seen, and each shard stops at ${K}` : `${fmt(r.matched)} matches seen${r.skipped ? ` · ${fmt(r.skipped)} skipped by block maximums` : ''}`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${r.ms.toFixed(1)} ms`;
      const times = r.per.map((p: any) => p.ms); const worst = times.indexOf(Math.max(...times));
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = S === 1 ? 'one index, one shard' : `slowest is shard ${worst + 1} (${times[worst].toFixed(1)} ms) · one index would take ${one.ms.toFixed(1)} ms`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = truth.length ? `${complete} of ${truth.length}` : 'no results';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = truth.length ? `${usedN} of ${S} shards answered · compared with a single full index` : 'nothing matches';
      const setC = (b: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(b).style.setProperty('--c', c);
      setC('[data-b1]', r.scanned > best.scanned * WASTE_X ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); setC('[data-b2]', 'var(--accent)');
      setC('[data-b3]', 'var(--accent)'); setC('[data-b4]', truth.length && complete < truth.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      const top = Math.max(...times, BAR_MIN_MS);
      bars.forEach((b, i) => {
        b.row.hidden = i >= S; if (i >= S) return;
        b.fill.style.width = `${(times[i] / top) * 100}%`; b.ms.textContent = `${times[i].toFixed(2)} ms`;
        b.row.classList.toggle('slow', i === worst && S > 1); b.row.classList.toggle('cut', !r.used[i]);
      });
      const qset = new Set(r.qt.map((t: any) => t.term));
      rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        const h = r.merged[i]; row.li.hidden = !h; if (!h) return;
        row.sc.textContent = cfg.rank === 'none' ? `#${h.id}` : `#${h.id}  ${h.score.toFixed(2)}`;
        const toks = corpus[h.id]; let at = toks.findIndex((w) => qset.has(cfg.stem ? stem(w) : w)); at = Math.max(0, Math.min(at < 0 ? 0 : at - SNIPPET.before, toks.length - SNIPPET.len));
        const frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
        toks.slice(at, at + SNIPPET.len).forEach((w, j) => { const hit = qset.has(cfg.stem ? stem(w) : w); const n = hit ? document.createElement('b') : document.createElement('span'); n.textContent = w; frag.append(n, j < SNIPPET.len - 1 ? ' ' : ''); });
        row.tx.replaceChildren(frag);
      });
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const parts: string[] = []; let bad = false;
      if (!r.qt.length) { parts.push('Nothing to search for: every word was a stop word.'); bad = true; }
      else if (!truth.length) {
        bad = true;
        const hasStop = !cfg.stop && cfg.q.split(' ').some((w) => STOPSET.has(w));
        parts.push(cfg.type === 'phrase' && hasStop ? 'No document has these words side by side. The stop word counts as part of the phrase here, so try removing stop words.'
          : !cfg.stem ? 'No document matches. Without stemming the index holds the words exactly as written, so a query word like searching only finds searching. Turn stemming on.'
          : cfg.type === 'phrase' ? 'No document has these words side by side, in this order.' : 'No document contains all of these words.');
      } else {
        if (r.scanned > best.scanned * WASTE_X) { bad = true; parts.push(`The query read ${fmt(r.scanned)} postings. Intersecting the shortest list first, with skip pointers, would read ${fmt(best.scanned)}, and the answer would be the same.`); }
        else parts.push(`The query read ${fmt(r.scanned)} postings${r.scanned > best.scanned ? ` (${fmt(best.scanned)} is the least with this setup)` : ', the least this setup allows'} to find ${fmt(r.matched)} matches${cfg.rank === 'none' ? '' : ` and scored ${fmt(r.scored)}`}.`);
        if (S > 1) parts.push(`The slowest of ${S} shards (shard ${worst + 1}) sets the time: ${r.ms.toFixed(1)} ms against ${one.ms.toFixed(1)} ms for one index.`);
        if (complete < truth.length) { bad = true; parts.push(`The top ${K} is incomplete: ${S - usedN} slow shard${S - usedN === 1 ? ' was' : 's were'} left out, so only ${complete} of the real top ${truth.length} were returned.`); }
      }
      out.classList.toggle('bad', bad); out.textContent = parts.join(' ');
    }
    let raf = 0; const schedule = () => { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(() => { raf = 0; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
